 "path": "continual_arc_notes.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC lesson: full 9-lines recoloring

Observed task pattern (demo: 24x4): locate every complete horizontal row or vertical column made entirely of 9s, and recolor every cell of those complete lines to 2. Leave all other cells unchanged. In the demo the all-9 column and complete all-9 rows became 2s; partial/noisy 9s remained 9. On the 26x23 test, the complete lines were rows 10 and 26 and columns 10, 16, 19, and 23 (1-based). Correct output replaces every cell along each such line, including any apparent non-9 entries if the line criterion identifies it; verify each full line carefully against the input before submitting.

General tactic: scan for rows/columns uniformly 9; change entire qualifying lines to 2, preserve everything else. Don't color isolated 9s or assume only one vertical line. A successful answer confirmed this rule."
